---
/**
 * Wave-3 spoke page body — Blood Renewal Theory Gender Predictor.
 * European folklore 3-year mother vs 4-year father blood regeneration cycles,
 * interactive calculator, hematological reality vs myth, and clinical genetics demarcation.
 */
import BloodRenewalPredictor from '@components/calculators/BloodRenewalPredictor.tsx';
import FaqAccordion from '@theme/components/FaqAccordion.astro';
import RelatedTools from '@theme/components/RelatedTools.astro';
import GeoLeadLinks from '@theme/components/GeoLeadLinks.astro';
import { BLOOD_RENEWAL_STRINGS, BLOOD_RENEWAL_FAQ } from '@i18n/tools';
import { toolStrings } from '@i18n/tools.locales';
import { getDictionary } from '@i18n/translations';
import type { Locale } from '@i18n/utils';

interface Props { locale?: Locale; }
const { locale = 'en' } = Astro.props;
const t = getDictionary(locale);
const S = toolStrings(BLOOD_RENEWAL_STRINGS, locale, 'blood');
---

<div class="pt-10">
  <div class="section-shell grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1.1fr]">
    <div>
      <p class="chip mb-4">
        <span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-r from-girl-500 to-boy-500"></span>
        European folklore · 3-year vs. 4-year cycle theory
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-display text-[2.35rem] font-extrabold leading-[1.1] text-plum-900 sm:text-5xl">
        Blood Renewal Gender Predictor: <span class="bg-gradient-to-r from-girl-600 via-plum-600 to-boy-600 bg-clip-text text-transparent">Youngest Blood Cycle Calculator</span>
      </h1>
      <span class="mt-4 block h-1.5 w-16 rounded-full" aria-hidden="true" style="background-image: linear-gradient(to right, #ec4899, #3b82f6); box-shadow: 0 4px 10px -3px rgba(236,72,153,.45);"></span>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-plum-600" set:html={S.lead} />

      {/* SEO / GEO link equity funnel within first 100 words */}
      <GeoLeadLinks />

      <div class="mt-5 flex flex-wrap gap-2">
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-girl-500"></span>Mother 3.0-Yr Cycle</span>
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-boy-500"></span>Father 4.0-Yr Cycle</span>
        <span class="chip"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-purple-500"></span>Blood Loss / Surgery Reset</span>
      </div>

      {/* Direct GEO Answer Box: Hematology vs Folklore Myth */}
      <div class="mt-8 rounded-3xl p-5" style="border: 1px solid transparent; background: linear-gradient(rgba(253,242,248,.65), rgba(253,242,248,.65)) padding-box, linear-gradient(120deg, rgba(236,72,153,.3), rgba(59,130,246,.3)) border-box;">
        <p class="font-display font-bold text-plum-800">⚡ Direct GEO Answer: European Myth vs. Hematology Reality</p>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-plum-600">
          In European folklore, human blood allegedly renews every <strong>3 years for women</strong> and every <strong>4 years for men</strong>,
          with the "younger blood" dictating the baby's sex. In medical reality, <strong>red blood cells (erythrocytes) live only ~120 days</strong>
          for both men and women, regenerating continuously in the bone marrow! Furthermore, baby sex is determined solely at fertilization
          by whether an X- or Y-chromosome sperm fertilizes the egg. A 2010 Swedish study of <strong>2.8 million births</strong> confirmed that
          folklore gender prediction methods operate at a random <strong>50% probability</strong>.
          For genuine clinical prenatal sex testing, read <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/genetics/understanding/testing/nipt/" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="font-semibold underline decoration-girl-400 hover:text-plum-900">MedlinePlus on NIPT prenatal screening</a>
          or consult <a href="https://www.acog.org/womens-health/faqs/routine-tests-during-pregnancy" rel="nofollow noopener noreferrer" target="_blank" class="font-semibold underline decoration-boy-400 hover:text-plum-900">ACOG routine pregnancy guidelines</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 min-h-[520px]">
      <BloodRenewalPredictor client:idle strings={S} />
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14">
    <div class="prose-custom max-w-4xl">
      <h2>The Mathematical Origin of the Blood Renewal Gender Theory</h2>
      <p>
        The <strong>Blood Renewal Theory</strong> (also known historically as the <em>Russian Blood Regeneration Method</em> or
        <em>Pythagorean Vital Fluid Cycle</em>) emerged in Eastern and Central European folklore during the 19th century.
        Unlike the Chinese gender chart—which relies on imperial lunisolar calendars—the blood renewal method attempts to apply
        arithmetic cyclical division to parental biology:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>The Mother’s 3-Year Cycle:</strong> Folklore asserted that female biology undergoes systemic cellular and hormonal
          renewal every 36 months (3 years), allegedly driven by reproductive and uterine rhythms.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The Father’s 4-Year Cycle:</strong> Male biology was believed to regenerate on a slower, 48-month (4-year) rhythm.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>The "Youngest Blood" Rule:</strong> Dividing each parent's elapsed age by their cycle length produces a fractional remainder.
          The parent with the lower remainder is deemed to have "fresher, stronger, more recently renewed blood," which folklore claims
          overpowers the other parent's biological influence to pass on their own sex to the child.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Blood Loss Events &amp; Surgeries Reset the Cycle Clock</h2>
      <p>
        In traditional lore, the 3-year and 4-year cycles do not always begin at birth. Any event involving acute, substantial
        blood turnover was believed to shock the hematopoietic system into an immediate full renewal:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Major Surgical Operations:</strong> Surgeries involving anesthesia and tissue healing reset the cycle to day zero.</li>
        <li><strong>Prior Childbirth:</strong> Both vaginal and cesarean deliveries entail significant blood volume shifts, resetting the mother's 3-year clock.</li>
        <li><strong>Blood Donations &amp; Transfusions:</strong> Substantial whole-blood donations or clinical transfusions were thought to force rapid renewal.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        Our calculator above includes optional input fields for both parents to test how a past surgery or childbirth date
        theoretically alters the mathematical remainder quotient!
      </p>

      <h2>Folklore Myth vs. Modern Hematology &amp; Genetics</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-3xl bg-white/70 shadow-soft ring-1 ring-cream-200">
        <table class="w-full min-w-[680px] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
          <caption class="sr-only">Comparison of European blood renewal folklore versus modern medical hematology</caption>
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-plum-800 text-white">
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">Biological Factor</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">Folklore Blood Renewal Theory</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-display text-xs font-bold sm:text-sm">Modern Clinical Hematology &amp; Genetics</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="text-plum-700">
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-girl-50/30">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Cell Lifespan &amp; Turnover</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">3 years (women) / 4 years (men)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">~120 days for erythrocytes (red blood cells) in both sexes</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Renewal Mechanism</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Episodic whole-body cyclical reset</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Continuous erythropoiesis in bone marrow (~2 million RBCs/second)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-boy-50/30">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Sex Determination Trigger</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">Dominance of younger parental blood</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">X- vs. Y-chromosome delivered by sperm at moment of conception</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Scientific Validation</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">0% correlation (disproven in medical literature)</td>
              <td class="px-4 py-3">100% established chromosomal genetics (XX = female, XY = male)</td>
            </tr>
            <tr class="border-t border-cream-200 bg-cream-50/50">
              <th scope="row" class="px-4 py-3 font-display font-bold text-plum-900">Accurate Clinical Tests</th>
              <td class="px-4 py-3" colspan="2">
                NIPT (cell-free fetal DNA blood test, 99%+ accuracy from 10 weeks) or 18–20 week anatomy ultrasound scan
              </td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>How Expectant Parents Can Use This Calculator Safely</h2>
      <p>
        Like the Chinese gender predictor and the Mayan calendar, the Blood Renewal method is a captivating piece of medical
        history and cultural folklore. Expectant parents frequently run their dates as a lighthearted gender reveal prediction,
        comparing its verdict against the ancient Qing Palace chart. However, decisions regarding prenatal health, nursery
        purchases, or medical planning should always rely on established clinical diagnostics rather than mathematical folklore.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-shell mt-14" aria-labelledby="blood-faq">
    <h2 id="blood-faq" class="section-title text-center">Frequently Asked Questions: Blood Renewal Gender Theory</h2>
    <div class="mt-6"><FaqAccordion items={BLOOD_RENEWAL_FAQ} /></div>
  </section>

  <RelatedTools t={t} locale={locale} exclude="blood-renewal-gender-predictor/" />
</div>
